 "text": "Substations \n Technical Procedure\n\nIntroduction\nThis procedure details \n the items, which are checked every 5 years Y5. They include testing and major \n maintenance P2. In addition to the procedures listed, it is expected the \n checks, which are done more frequently, would also be completed at this \n time.\nSafety Precautions\nPersonnel carrying out the maintenance \n should be trained and qualified or directly supervised by some one who \n is.\nTools and Equipment\nBituminous paint and suitable paint \n brushes for repainting the internal surface of the tank\nSpecial Safety Precautions\nDo not use the mobile crane for the \n actual lift, but attach a rope block and use the crane hook as a gin \n pole.\nEnvironmental Recommendation\nIf you are going to repaint the \n outside surface of the tank by using spray gun for painting process. Try to \n follow the following instructions to reduce wastes and protect your \n health:\nRecycle over spray.\nWork to be Carried Out\nInspect the moving contact (61 Fig 4):\nIf more than 1/3 of the contact surface is damaged it should be changed.\nChanging the Moving Contact\nInspect the segment contact (51 Fig 4) and its springs for this inspection \n it is necessary to remove the cap of the bearer (60 Fig 4) by means of a \n special pipe wrench.\nChanging the Fixed \nContact\nNote:\nClosing time: 0. 25 sec, \n Opening time: 0.07 sec\nRecord all results on maintenance card.\n............................................................................................................................................................\nLocation: \nEquipment code: \nChecked by: \nDate: \nSignature:\nFigure 1 Compressed air Operation \ndiagram\n1\nContainer\n11a\nPneumatic impactor for \n closing\n2\nSupport \n insulators\n11b\nPneumatic impactor for \n opening\n3\nPorcelain \n tube\n12\n13-pole pilot \n switch\n4\nPorcelain \n spindle\n13\nWorking \n cylinder\n5\nChamber \n casing\n14a\nRelief for \n closing\n6\nIsolator \